  "prefLabel": "Env-A 705.01 Definition",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 705.01 Definition. For the purposes of this part, “VOC or RTAP emissions unit” means an emission unit located at a stationary source, area source, or device that emits any volatile organic compound (VOC) or regulated toxic air pollutant (RTAP) from a non-combustion process.\n\nSource. #12649, eff 10-24-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a700.html"
